---
description: Local infrastructure isolation and documentation verification
globs: "infrastructure/**,scripts/**,docs/**,Makefile,**/README.md"
alwaysApply: false
---
Use project-scoped Compose volumes/networks and loopback published ports. No external project database reuse.
Never delete state or use Docker prune. PostgreSQL init and Keycloak import are first-boot only; changes require controlled migrations/reconciliation.
Local tooling: Makefile targets wrap mvnw, npm, docker compose, or short Bash scripts in scripts/local. Scripts use `set -euo pipefail`, must pass `bash -n`, never print secrets, and never overwrite .env or .local/ silently. No Python.
Keep `make help` descriptions accurate to the exact Maven/npm goal they run (test vs verify). Avoid duplicate work across aggregate targets.
Update docs/service-status.md, docs/progress.md, docs/verification.md and affected local guide after changes; keep docs/local-development.md command tables in sync with the Makefile.
Distinguish source implemented, static checked, tests passed, runtime verified, blocked, and planned.
Document exact commands and expected observations, not imagined evidence.
Do not disable TLS/JWT validation or authentication to make a smoke test succeed.
